.TH "PB-ENV-TEAM-CREATE" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-env-team-create - Create an encrypted ENV team scope


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb env team create <team> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Create an encrypted ENV team scope

.PP
Create an encrypted scope for the selected team. Team globals sync to authorized Team devices. Members decrypt Team globals through encrypted key grants, while their private global and device values remain isolated in the Team workspace.

.PP
Team ENV scopes have their own encrypted keys and explicit account grants. Rotation preserves values while replacing access keys; reset discards values. Review the confirmation and affected members before changing custody.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for create

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-env-team(1)\fP
